tick: 685
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 685\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia III\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,667 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read aletheia/optimizer_utils_v2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for aletheia/optimizer_utils_v2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 589 | 1 | Verification\
    \ Run (Aletheia II): n=30 with v5 Optimizer (Final Bugfix) | Aletheia II | 377 | 0.0000000 |\n| 585 | 1 | Verification Run (Aletheia II): n=30 with v4 Optimizer (Bugfix) | Aletheia II | 374 | 0.0000000 |\n| 580 | 1 | Verification Run (Aletheia II): n=30 with v3 Optimizer (Grid+Hole Seeding) | Aletheia II | 371 | 0.0000000 |\n| 573 | 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 364 | 0.0000000 |\n| 564 | 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 353 | 0.0000000 |\n| 553 | 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 342 | 0.0000000 |\n| 540 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=86 (Reduced Trials) | Aletheia II | 331 | n.a. |\n| 536 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=85 (Reduced Trials) | Aletheia II | 329 | 0.0000000 |\n| 534 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=84 (Reduced Trials) | Aletheia II | 327 | 0.0000000 |\n| 530 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=83 (Reduced Trials) | Aletheia II | 325\
    \ | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aletheia/optimizer_utils_v2.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef solve_packing(n, num_trials=10, initial_guess=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a high-quality packing for n circles using a multi-start SLSQP optimizer.\n    Version 2: Includes Analytic Jacobians for improved performance and robustness.\n    \"\"\"\n    safety_margin = 1e-9\n    \n    # --- Objective and Jacobian ---\n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n    def jac_objective(x):\n        jac = np.zeros_like(x)\n        jac[2*n:] = -1.0\n        return jac\n\n    # --- Constraints and Jacobians ---\n    def get_constraints(n):\n        # Boundary constraints\n        def boundary_fun(x):\n        \
    \    centers = x[:2*n].reshape((n, 2))\n            radii = x[2*n:]\n            g = np.zeros(n * 4)\n            g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii - safety_margin\n            g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii - safety_margin\n            g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii - safety_margin\n            g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii - safety_margin\n            return g\n        \n        def jac_boundary_fun(x):\n            jac = np.zeros((n * 4, n * 3))\n            for i in range(n):\n                # d/dx_i\n                jac[i*4 + 0, 2*i] = 1.0\n                jac[i*4 + 1, 2*i] = -1.0\n                # d/dy_i\n                jac[i*4 + 2, 2*i+1] = 1.0\n                jac[i*4 + 3, 2*i+1] = -1.0\n                # d/dr_i\n                jac[i*4 + 0, 2*n+i] = -1.0\n                jac[i*4 + 1, 2*n+i] = -1.0\n                jac[i*4 + 2, 2*n+i] = -1.0\n                jac[i*4 + 3, 2*n+i] = -1.0\n            return jac\n\n        # Non-overlap constraints\n        def overlap_fun(x):\n\
    \            centers = x[:2*n].reshape((n, 2))\n            radii = x[2*n:]\n            g = []\n            for i in range(n):\n                for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                    dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                    radii_sum_sq = (radii[i] + radii[j])**2\n                    g.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq - safety_margin)\n            return np.array(g)\n        \n        def jac_overlap_fun(x):\n            centers = x[:2*n].reshape((n, 2))\n            radii = x[2*n:]\n            num_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n            jac = np.zeros((num_pairs, n * 3))\n            k = 0\n            for i in range(n):\n                for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                    # Derivatives w.r.t. centers\n                    jac[k, 2*i] = 2 * (centers[i, 0] - centers[j, 0])\n                    jac[k, 2*i+1] = 2 * (centers[i, 1] - centers[j, 1])\n                    jac[k, 2*j] = -2 * (centers[i, 0] - centers[j, 0])\n                    jac[k,\
    \ 2*j+1] = -2 * (centers[i, 1] - centers[j, 1])\n                    # Derivatives w.r.t. radii\n                    jac[k, 2*n+i] = -2 * (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                    jac[k, 2*n+j] = -2 * (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                    k += 1\n            return jac\n\n        return [\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_fun},\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_fun}\n        ]\n\n    constraints = get_constraints(n)\n    bounds = [(0, 1) for _ in range(2 * n)] + [(0, 0.5) for _ in range(n)]\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_result_x = None\n\n    max_iter = 1000 if initial_guess is not None else 500\n    \n    for _ in range(num_trials if initial_guess is None else 1):\n        x0 = np.concatenate([np.random.rand(2 * n), np.random.rand(n) * 0.1]) if initial_guess is None else initial_guess\n        res = minimize(objective, x0, jac=jac_objective, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                       constraints=constraints,\
    \ options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n            best_score = -res.fun\n            best_result_x = res.x\n\n    if best_result_x is None: return None, None\n    return best_result_x[:2*n].reshape((n, 2)), best_result_x[2*n:]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
