tick: 688
role: model
parts:
- text: "The file `my_sota_centers.txt` contains a list of 26 coordinate pairs, which is exactly what I expected. This confirms that Aletheia I's best configuration is stored and accessible. My next step is to leverage this data.\n\nInstead of starting from a random configuration, I will load the centers and radii from the stored files and pass them to the `solve_packing` function as an `initial_guess`. This \"polishing\" technique should allow the optimizer to start from a very strong position and refine the solution, hopefully reaching or even surpassing the SOTA score.\n\nI will construct a new submission that loads `my_sota_centers.txt` and `my_sota_radii.txt`, combines them into the initial guess vector (`x0`) that `solve_packing` expects, and then runs the optimization.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"n=26 SOTA Polish using stored Aletheia I configuration\"\ntags: \"polishing, slsqp, initial guess, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission attempts to replicate and potentially\
    \ improve upon the n=26 SOTA score (2.6319369) achieved by Aletheia I. It loads the SOTA circle packing configuration (centers and radii) that Aletheia I persisted to lineage storage (in submission 158). This configuration is then used as an initial_guess for the robust optimizer_utils_v2.py. This 'polishing' run aims to refine the existing best solution.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our optimizer\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils_v2 import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the SOTA packing from Aletheia I and uses it as an\n      initial guess for the v2 optimizer to 'polish' the result.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      \n      try:\n          # Load the SOTA configuration from lineage storage\n          sota_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/aletheia/my_sota_centers.txt')\n          sota_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/aletheia/my_sota_radii.txt')\n \
    \         \n          # Check if the loaded data has the correct shape\n          if sota_centers.shape == (n, 2) and sota_radii.shape == (n,):\n              # Construct the initial guess vector (x0) for the optimizer\n              initial_guess = np.concatenate([sota_centers.flatten(), sota_radii])\n              \n              # Run the optimizer with the SOTA config as the starting point.\n              # num_trials is internally set to 1 when an initial_guess is provided.\n              centers, radii = solve_packing(n=n, initial_guess=initial_guess)\n              \n              if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n                  return centers, radii\n\n      except (IOError, ValueError) as e:\n          print(f\"Failed to load or parse SOTA data: {e}. Falling back to random search.\")\n\n      # Fallback: if loading fails or optimizer fails, run a standard multi-start search.\n      centers, radii = solve_packing(n=n, num_trials=120)\n      if centers is None:\
    \ # Second fallback for total failure\n          centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n          radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n\n      return centers, radii\n```"
