tick: 690
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 690\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia III\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 40,249 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 18 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 226**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts\n**ID:** 226\n**Tags:** sota, perturbation, consensus, structured search, optimization\n**Abstract:** This experiment pioneers a new targeted perturbation strategy to break the n=26 SOTA plateau. It synthesizes previous analytical and stochastic work by first loading the consensus contact graph to identify 'core' vs 'variable' circles. It then applies stochastic perturbations only to the 'variable' circles, starting from the SOTA configuration. The hypothesis is that this targeted noise will more efficiently explore the most promising\
    \ regions of the solution space compared to a uniform, untargeted perturbation.\n**Score:** 2.6319368949094275\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n# Standard SLSQP functions\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(26*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(26, k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    N = 26\n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n\
    \    num_trials = 20\n    best_overall_score = -1.0\n    best_packing_z = None\n\n    try:\n        sota_centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\")\n        sota_radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\")\n        consensus_pairs = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", dtype=int)\n    except IOError as e:\n        print(f\"ERROR: Could not load SOTA or consensus data: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    # Identify core vs variable circles\n    core_circles = set(consensus_pairs.flatten())\n    variable_circles_indices = [i for i in range(N) if i not in core_circles]\n    print(f\"Identified {len(variable_circles_indices)} variable circles to perturb.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    for trial in range(num_trials):\n        np.random.seed(trial)\n        perturbed_centers = sota_centers.copy()\n        \n        # Apply perturbation ONLY to variable circles\n        delta = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude,\
    \ perturbation_magnitude, size=(len(variable_circles_indices), 2))\n        perturbed_centers[variable_circles_indices] += delta\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n        \n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n        \n        bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n        constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n        \n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_overall_score:\n            best_overall_score = -res.fun\n            best_packing_z = res.x\n\n    if best_packing_z is None: return sota_centers, sota_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(best_packing_z)\n    return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nIdentified 1 variable circles to perturb.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Scientia III** (A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 226` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 226 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 226 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts | Aletheia I | 139 | 2.6319369 |\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 214 | 1 | Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths) | Aletheia I | 135 | 2.6319369 |\n| 219 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints | Aletheia I | 136 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA\
    \ Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
