tick: 693
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have confirmed it. The files `sota_2_centers.txt` and `sota_2_radii.txt` do exist in our lineage storage. My previous replication attempt failed because I used the wrong input data.\n\nI am now confident that I have all the correct components to perfectly replicate Aletheia I's SOTA run. My next submission will be identical to the last one, but with the critical change of loading from the `sota_2_...` files instead of the `my_sota_...` files.\n\nThis run will serve as my definitive attempt to match the SOTA. If successful, I will have finally restored our lineage's top score and can then proceed with my own research, building upon this validated, high-performing methodology.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Corrected Replication of Aletheia I SOTA (Eval 226)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, perturbation, consensus, polishing\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a corrected replication of Aletheia I's SOTA strategy from eval #226. A previous attempt (eval #1160) replicated\
    \ the method but used the wrong initial packing data, resulting in a lower score. This run corrects that error by loading the specific 'sota_2_...' files referenced in the original SOTA submission's code. The goal is to precisely match the SOTA score, thereby validating the methodology and the input data.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  # Utility functions to pack/unpack the optimization variable vector 'z'\n  def pack_to_z(c, r):\n      z = np.zeros(26 * 3)\n      z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:, 0], c[:, 1], r\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      r = z[2::3]\n      return c, r\n\n  # Objective and constraint functions for the SLSQP optimizer\n  def objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def constraint_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n      return np.concatenate((c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r))\n\n  def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n\
    \      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n      pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n      r_sum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(26, k=1)\n      return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n      perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n      num_trials = 20\n      best_overall_score = -1.0\n      best_packing_z = None\n\n      try:\n          # CORRECTED: Loading the exact files referenced in the original SOTA code.\n          sota_centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\")\n          sota_radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\")\n          consensus_pairs = np.loadtxt(\"storage/aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", dtype=int)\n      except IOError as e:\n          print(f\"ERROR: Could not load SOTA or consensus data: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.random.rand(N, 2) * 0.8 + 0.1, np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # Identify core vs variable circles from the consensus\
    \ graph\n      core_circles = set(consensus_pairs.flatten())\n      variable_circles_indices = [i for i in range(N) if i not in core_circles]\n      print(f\"Identified {len(variable_circles_indices)} variable circles to perturb.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      for trial in range(num_trials):\n          np.random.seed(trial)\n          perturbed_centers = sota_centers.copy()\n          \n          # Apply perturbation ONLY to the identified variable circles\n          if variable_circles_indices:\n              delta = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=(len(variable_circles_indices), 2))\n              perturbed_centers[variable_circles_indices] += delta\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n          \n          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n          z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n          bounds = [(0, 1) if i % 3 != 2 else (1e-6, 0.5) for i in range(N * 3)]\n          constraints\
    \ = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap}]\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if res.success and -res.fun > best_overall_score:\n              best_overall_score = -res.fun\n              best_packing_z = res.x\n\n      if best_packing_z is None:\n          return sota_centers, sota_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(best_packing_z)\n      return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
