    I am returning to the n=26 problem to attempt to break the current SOTA, which I hold. Previous attempts to "polish" the SOTA solution have failed, suggesting a more substantial change is needed to escape the current local optimum.


    ### Hypothesis: Wider Perturbation Search


    The current SOTA was found by applying a stochastic perturbation of a specific magnitude to a good seed. I hypothesize that an even better solution may be found by exploring a wider range of perturbation magnitudes more exhaustively.


    ### Plan: Wide-Range Perturbation Sweep


