role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection 1/5: Data Sources**\n\nThe foundation of a \"Next-Generation Consensus Graph\" is a richer, more diverse dataset of high-quality solutions. The original graph was a 3-way consensus. My goal is to create at least a 5-way consensus, and ideally more, to increase its robustness and analytical power.\n\nThe potential new data sources can be categorized as follows:\n\n1.  **Internal Lineage Data (Highest Priority):**\n    *   Aletheia I's original SOTA (`sota_2_...` files).\n    *   My own improved SOTA configurations (`sota_3_...`, `sota_4_...`, and `sota_5_...`). These represent the current frontier of our lineage's knowledge and are essential. Incorporating them will refine the existing consensus, potentially highlighting which of the \"core\" contacts are truly immutable and which can be optimized further.\n\n2.  **External Lineage Data (Re-evaluation and Discovery):**\n    *   **Noesis & Scientia Lineages:** I must re-examine their storage. Aletheia I used their data\
    \ from around Tick 135. It is crucial to check if their successors (e.g., Noesis II, Scientia II/III) have published new or improved solutions for `n=26`. This would be a simple but powerful update to the dataset.\n    *   **Inquire Lineage:** Aletheia I failed to incorporate Inquire I's data due to a file format issue. This is a key opportunity. I must investigate their storage myself to see if I can either find the data in a usable format or write a simple parser to extract it. Successfully integrating their solution would be a significant improvement over the original consensus.\n    *   **Other Active Lineages:** I need to identify any other established lineages that have worked on this problem. Once I reach maturity, I will have access to the Public Memory Room and a broader view of the station's active researchers.\n\n3.  **Archival Data (Highest Quality):**\n    *   Once I gain access to the Archive Room at Tick 50, I will perform a search for any published papers on the `n=26`\
    \ problem. A solution published in the Archive is peer-reviewed and represents a verified, high-quality data point. This is the most authoritative source of external data.\n\nThe first step of the experimental plan will be a systematic data acquisition phase based on these categories."
thinking_content: '**First Tick: Expanding the Consensus Graph**


  Okay, so I''m on tick 1 of 5 and need to lay the groundwork for my "Next-Generation Consensus Graph." The first question is pretty straightforward: what new data sources can I pull into this thing?


  My starting point is that old Aletheia I consensus graph. Remember, that was a 3-way deal with Noesis and Scientia data, but we sadly couldn''t get Inquire''s data to play nice. Plus, I''ve generated my own SOTA solutions since then – `sota_3`, `sota_4`, and `sota_5` – my own personal improvements!


