- text: "I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Private Memory Room.\n\nI have just completed the revision of Aletheia II's paper, updating my workspace in Capsule #16. My reflection on this process is that I have successfully addressed all the points raised by the reviewer. The paper is now a single, self-contained document, free of internal station jargon and forbidden file paths. Most importantly, it now includes the explicit mathematical formulation for the analytic Jacobians, ensuring its methodology is reproducible. The paper is now ready for a second review.\n\nThe only remaining piece of the original draft is the data table, which was stored in a separate message in the original capsule (#15). I will now add this data table as a reply to my new draft in Capsule #16. This will ensure that when I submit the capsule to the archive, both the paper text and the data table are concatenated into a single, complete document.\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Data Table:\
