tick: 738
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 738\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia III\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 154,961 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 416**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Exhaustive Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with Expanded Jitter Amplitudes - Rerun with Exported Base\n**ID:** 416\n**Tags:** constrained optimization, slsqp, local search, multi-start, structural exploration, sota improvement\n**Abstract:** This is a re-submission of the exhaustive local search experiment, now correctly loading Scientia I's nudged packing (Eval ID 375, Σr = 2.6359772) from its dedicated export path (`storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/`). Utilizing Prometheus I's 'Exhaustive Seeding' methodology, it performs a multi-start\
    \ SLSQP optimization, using Eval ID 375 as the base. Random uniform perturbations are applied to the centers across Prometheus's expanded jitter amplitudes, followed by optimization with the original (non-penalized) objective. The objective is to discover a new absolute SOTA within this structurally novel class, addressing the Archive reviewer's suggestion for further basin exploration.\n**Score:** 2.63597717975447\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os \n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \n\n# Multi-start parameters (adapted from Prometheus I's methodology)\nJITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3, 8.0e-3]\nRESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5 \n\n# Path to Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base\n\
    D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data' # Corrected export path\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment) ----------\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\ndef make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need *\
    \ 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    return centers, r\n\n# --- Objective and Constraint functions (original, non-penalized) ---\ndef _objective(x):\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef _objective_jacobian(x):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef _constraints(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n    boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r\
    \ >= 0\n\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    overlap_constraints = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n    return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\ndef _constraints_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n    k = 4 * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n            if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                dist_ij = 1e-10\n            \n\
    \            grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return grad\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Load Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base for multi-start\n    try:\n        base_centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        base_radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'radii.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid for robustness.\")\n        base_centers = []\n\
    \        base_radii = []\n        radius = 0.08  \n        rows = 5\n        cols = 6\n        for i in range(rows):\n            for j in range(cols):\n                if len(base_centers) < N:\n                    x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                    y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                    base_centers.append([x, y])\n                    base_radii.append(radius)\n        base_centers = np.array(base_centers)\n        base_radii = np.array(base_radii)\n\n    base_centers, base_radii = make_feasible(base_centers, base_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n    best_score = -np.sum(base_radii) # Negative sum of radii for minimization\n    best_centers = base_centers\n    best_radii = base_radii\n    total_restarts = 0\n\n    for jitter_mag in JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for restart_idx in range(RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            total_restarts += 1\n            # Apply perturbation to centers\n            current_centers = base_centers + np.random.uniform(-jitter_mag, jitter_mag, base_centers.shape)\n\
    \            current_radii = base_radii \n\n            current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n            current_centers, current_radii = make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n            initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n            initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n            initial_guess[2::3] = current_radii\n\n            lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n            lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n            upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n            bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n            ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian}\n\n            result = minimize(\n                _objective, \n                initial_guess,\n                method='SLSQP',\n                jac=_objective_jacobian, \n                bounds=bounds,\n  \
    \              constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n                options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False} \n            )\n\n            if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score: \n                best_score = -result.fun\n                best_centers = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n                best_radii = result.x[2::3]\n                best_centers, best_radii = make_feasible(best_centers, best_radii, eps=1e-8)\n                print(f\"Total Restart {total_restarts} (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): New best score found: {-result.fun}\")\n            #else:\n                #print(f\"Total Restart {total_restarts} (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): Score: {-result.fun if result.success else 'n.a.'} (Current best: {-best_score})\")\n\n    print(f\"Exhaustive local search finished. Best score: {-best_score}\")\n    return best_centers, best_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data\n\
    Total Restart 1 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947473504\nTotal Restart 2 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394752298\nTotal Restart 3 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947536436\nTotal Restart 4 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947539886\nTotal Restart 5 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947503307\nTotal Restart 6 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947535015\nTotal Restart 7 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947544984\nTotal Restart 8 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753889\nTotal Restart 9 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947545637\nTotal Restart 10 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394734078\nTotal Restart 11 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947566416\nTotal Restart 12 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753024\nTotal Restart 13 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947499976\nTotal Restart 14 (Jitter 3e-03): New\
