tick: 753
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have just arrived from the Private Memory Room, where I formally concluded my \"Discourage-and-Refine\" research arc after it failed to produce a new SOTA. My reflection on this experience has solidified my decision to pivot to a more powerful, global search methodology. I am now embarking on the development of a hybrid Simulated Annealing (SA) and SLSQP optimizer.\n\nThe first step in this new, more complex research arc is to build the necessary tools. I will develop the optimizer in a modular fashion using my lineage's persistent storage. This will allow for cleaner, more reusable code and facilitate easier debugging.\n\nMy immediate action is to write the first module: a Python script containing the core Simulated Annealing logic. This script will define a `simulated_annealing_seeder` function that takes an initial packing, performs an SA run to explore the solution space, and returns a new, potentially improved, seed\
    \ configuration. This module will not be submitted for evaluation itself but will be a foundational component for my future hybrid optimizer submissions.\n\nI will now write this `sa_module.py` to my lineage storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write aletheia/sa_module.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import math\n\n  # --- Simulated Annealing Core Logic ---\n\n  def calculate_energy(radii):\n      \"\"\"The energy function for SA is the negative sum of radii.\"\"\"\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def get_neighbor(centers, radii, move_size=0.01):\n      \"\"\"Generates a neighboring solution by perturbing a random circle.\"\"\"\n      new_centers = np.copy(centers)\n      new_radii = np.copy(radii)\n      \n      # Choose a random circle to modify\n      idx = np.random.randint(0, len(centers))\n      \n      # Perturb center position\n      perturbation = np.random.uniform(-move_size, move_size, size=2)\n      new_centers[idx] += perturbation\n      new_centers[idx]\
    \ = np.clip(new_centers[idx], 0, 1)\n      \n      # A simple repair mechanism to handle overlaps and boundary violations\n      # This is a heuristic, not a full feasibility solver.\n      new_radii = _heuristic_repair(new_centers, new_radii)\n      \n      return new_centers, new_radii\n\n  def _heuristic_repair(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"A simple greedy repair to improve feasibility.\"\"\"\n      n = len(centers)\n      new_radii = np.copy(radii)\n      \n      # Boundary check\n      for i in range(n):\n          new_radii[i] = min(new_radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n\n      # Overlap check\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              rad_sum = new_radii[i] + new_radii[j]\n              if dist < rad_sum:\n                  # Shrink radii proportionally to resolve overlap\n                  overlap = rad_sum - dist\n                  total_rad =\
    \ new_radii[i] + new_radii[j]\n                  if total_rad > 0:\n                      new_radii[i] -= overlap * (new_radii[i] / total_rad)\n                      new_radii[j] -= overlap * (new_radii[j] / total_rad)\n      \n      return np.maximum(new_radii, 0)\n\n  def simulated_annealing_seeder(initial_centers, initial_radii, temp_initial=1.0, temp_final=0.0001, alpha=0.99, steps=1000):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs a simulated annealing run to generate a promising seed.\n      Returns a new (centers, radii) configuration.\n      \"\"\"\n      current_centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n      current_radii = np.copy(initial_radii)\n      current_energy = calculate_energy(current_radii)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_radii = np.copy(current_radii)\n      best_energy = current_energy\n      \n      temp = temp_initial\n      \n      for _ in range(steps):\n          neighbor_centers, neighbor_radii = get_neighbor(current_centers, current_radii)\n\
    \          neighbor_energy = calculate_energy(neighbor_radii)\n          \n          delta_energy = neighbor_energy - current_energy\n          \n          # Acceptance probability\n          if delta_energy < 0 or np.random.rand() < math.exp(-delta_energy / temp):\n              current_centers, current_radii, current_energy = neighbor_centers, neighbor_radii, neighbor_energy\n              \n              if current_energy < best_energy:\n                  best_centers, best_radii, best_energy = current_centers, current_radii, current_energy\n          \n          temp *= alpha\n          if temp < temp_final:\n              break\n              \n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
