tick: 754
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully created the foundational module for my new Simulated Annealing research arc, `sa_module.py`, and saved it to my lineage's storage. This module contains the core logic for the SA process, which will act as a global \"seed generator\" in my planned hybrid optimizer.\n\nMy reflection on this first step is that it is a necessary but insufficient part of the final algorithm. The `sa_module.py` I've written uses a very simple, heuristic-based repair function to handle overlaps. While this is sufficient for the exploratory nature of SA, it will not produce a perfectly valid, high-precision solution. The true power of my new methodology will come from combining this global, approximate search with the precise, constraint-honoring power of the SLSQP optimizer.\n\nThe next step is to create the second part of the hybrid system: the refinement module. I have already developed and validated a powerful SLSQP refinement\
    \ script during my \"Nudge-and-Refine\" experiments. I will now adapt and generalize this code into a reusable module, `slsqp_refiner_module.py`, and write it to my storage. This module will take a seed configuration (like the one produced by my SA module) and perform an exhaustive local search to find the deepest possible optimum in its vicinity.\n\nBy creating these two distinct modules, I can then write a very clean final submission script that simply imports from both to execute the full \"SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine\" pipeline.\n\n/execute_action{storage write aletheia/slsqp_refiner_module.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  # --- SLSQP Refinement Core Logic ---\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n     \
    \ return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1) + 1e-15)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      r_new = np.copy(r)\n      for i in range(N): \n          r_new[i] = min(r_new[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10): \n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  if dist < r_new[i] + r_new[j]: \n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/(r_new[i] + r_new[j]))*(1.0-SAFETY); r_new[i]*=scale; r_new[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break \n      return c, np.maximum(r_new, 0)\n\n  def refine_with_slsqp(seed_centers, seed_radii, jitter_amps, restarts_per_amp):\n    \
    \  \"\"\"\n      Takes a seed configuration and performs an exhaustive, multi-start SLSQP refinement.\n      \"\"\"\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_centers, best_radii = None, None\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      # First, refine the original seed without jitter\n      initial_z_no_jitter = cr_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z_no_jitter, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n          best_score = -res.fun\n          c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n          best_centers, best_radii = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n\n      # Then, perform multi-start jitter refinement\n      for amp in jitter_amps:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amp):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp * 1e6) + i)\n           \
    \   jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=seed_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(seed_centers + jitter, R_MIN, 1 - R_MIN)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, seed_radii)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n                  best_score = -res.fun\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  best_centers, best_radii = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n      \n      if best_centers is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
