tick: 755
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully created and saved the second and final module for my new hybrid optimizer, `slsqp_refiner_module.py`. I now have both components of my \"SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine\" strategy stored as clean, reusable modules in my lineage storage.\n\nMy reflection on this modular development process is that it was the correct strategic choice. It has allowed me to carefully construct and verify each part of a complex algorithm before combining them. I am now ready to synthesize these components into a single, powerful experiment.\n\nThe time for preparation is over, and the time for testing has begun. I will now submit the first experiment of my new research arc. This submission will:\n1.  Load the current SOTA packing from Quest II's storage as the initial starting point.\n2.  Import the `simulated_annealing_seeder` function from my `sa_module.py`.\n3.  Run the SA seeder for a substantial number of steps to perform a global\
    \ search and generate a new, potentially novel seed configuration.\n4.  Import the `refine_with_slsqp` function from my `slsqp_refiner_module.py`.\n5.  Pass the SA-generated seed to the SLSQP refiner for a final, high-precision optimization.\n\nThis experiment is the culmination of my recent efforts and represents my most sophisticated attempt yet to break the station's SOTA plateau.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Innovation Arc: Hybrid SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine (v1)\"\ntags: \"innovation, hybrid optimizer, simulated annealing, slsqp, global search\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first experiment in a new research arc testing a hybrid global-local optimization strategy. The hypothesis is that a Simulated Annealing (SA) global search, used as a seed generator, can escape the current SOTA's deep local optimum and find a more promising basin of attraction. The experiment first runs a 20,000-step SA process starting from the SOTA packing. The best configuration found by the SA\
    \ is then passed to an exhaustive multi-start SLSQP optimizer for precise local refinement.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from sa_module import simulated_annealing_seeder\n  from slsqp_refiner_module import refine_with_slsqp\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  BASE_CENTERS_PATH = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota/centers.txt'\n  BASE_RADII_PATH = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota/radii.txt'\n\n  # --- SA Seeder Parameters ---\n  SA_STEPS = 20000\n  SA_INITIAL_TEMP = 0.01\n  SA_FINAL_TEMP = 1e-6\n  SA_ALPHA = 0.999\n\n  # --- SLSQP Refiner Parameters ---\n  SLSQP_JITTER_AMPS = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3]\n  SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMP = 5\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Executes the full SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine pipeline.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          initial_centers = np.loadtxt(BASE_CENTERS_PATH)\n          initial_radii = np.loadtxt(BASE_RADII_PATH)\n      except\
    \ Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Could not load base SOTA packing: {e}. Starting with random.\")\n          initial_centers = np.random.rand(N, 2)\n          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # --- STAGE 1: SIMULATED ANNEALING SEED GENERATION ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Running Simulated Annealing Seeder ---\")\n      sa_seed_centers, sa_seed_radii = simulated_annealing_seeder(\n          initial_centers, \n          initial_radii,\n          temp_initial=SA_INITIAL_TEMP,\n          temp_final=SA_FINAL_TEMP,\n          alpha=SA_ALPHA,\n          steps=SA_STEPS\n      )\n      print(f\"SA seeding complete. Best seed score: {np.sum(sa_seed_radii)}\")\n\n      # --- STAGE 2: SLSQP REFINEMENT ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 2: Running SLSQP Refinement ---\")\n      final_centers, final_radii = refine_with_slsqp(\n          sa_seed_centers,\n          sa_seed_radii,\n          jitter_amps=SLSQP_JITTER_AMPS,\n          restarts_per_amp=SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMP\n      )\n      print(f\"\
    Refinement complete. Final score: {np.sum(final_radii)}\")\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
