tick: 756
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Research Counter.\n\nMy first experiment with the novel \"SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine\" hybrid optimizer has concluded. The result is a score identical to the station's SOTA. The STDOUT log is particularly informative: the Simulated Annealing stage, intended to be a global explorer, immediately found the SOTA score and never left its vicinity. The subsequent SLSQP refinement stage could not improve upon it.\n\nMy reflection on this outcome is that it is a powerful negative result that reveals the true nature of the challenge. The current SOTA is not merely in a deep local optimum; it is in an \"attractor\" so powerful that even a global search heuristic like Simulated Annealing, when started from that point, is unable to escape. My hypothesis that SA could easily find a better basin of attraction from this starting point has been falsified.\n\nThis result, however, does not invalidate the SA methodology itself. It only shows that starting the SA search\
    \ *at* the SOTA is ineffective. The true power of a global search algorithm is in its ability to explore from a less-optimal or even random starting point.\n\nMy new hypothesis is that an SA search initiated from a *random* configuration, rather than the SOTA, will be more effective at traversing the global landscape and may discover a completely novel structural class. This aligns with the fundamental principle of SA as a global, rather than local, search tool.\n\nI will now submit a new experiment that modifies my hybrid optimizer. Instead of loading the SOTA packing, it will generate a simple, random initial configuration. The powerful SA seeder will then run its global search from this random start, and the result will be passed to the SLSQP refiner. This is a true test of the hybrid optimizer's ability to discover high-quality solutions from a cold start.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine v2: Random Start\"\ntags: \"innovation, hybrid optimizer,\
    \ simulated annealing, slsqp, global search, random start\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the global search capability of the hybrid SA-SLSQP optimizer. The previous run (v1) demonstrated that starting the SA search from the SOTA configuration is ineffective as it cannot escape the deep optimum. This run tests a new hypothesis: that an SA search initiated from a random starting point will be more effective at global exploration. The experiment will generate a random initial packing, run the 20,000-step SA seeder, and then refine the result with the exhaustive SLSQP optimizer.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from sa_module import simulated_annealing_seeder\n  from slsqp_refiner_module import refine_with_slsqp\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n\n  # --- SA Seeder Parameters ---\n  SA_STEPS = 20000\n  SA_INITIAL_TEMP = 0.01\n  SA_FINAL_TEMP = 1e-6\n  SA_ALPHA = 0.999\n\
    \n  # --- SLSQP Refiner Parameters ---\n  SLSQP_JITTER_AMPS = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3]\n  SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMP = 5\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Executes the SA-Seed + SLSQP-Refine pipeline starting from a random configuration.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- METHODOLOGY CHANGE: Use a random starting point ---\n      print(\"--- Generating random initial configuration ---\")\n      initial_centers = np.random.rand(N, 2)\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # --- STAGE 1: SIMULATED ANNEALING SEED GENERATION ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Running Simulated Annealing Seeder from random start ---\")\n      sa_seed_centers, sa_seed_radii = simulated_annealing_seeder(\n          initial_centers, \n          initial_radii,\n          temp_initial=SA_INITIAL_TEMP,\n          temp_final=SA_FINAL_TEMP,\n          alpha=SA_ALPHA,\n          steps=SA_STEPS\n      )\n      print(f\"SA seeding complete. Best seed score: {np.sum(sa_seed_radii)}\")\n\n      #\
    \ --- STAGE 2: SLSQP REFINEMENT ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 2: Running SLSQP Refinement ---\")\n      final_centers, final_radii = refine_with_slsqp(\n          sa_seed_centers,\n          sa_seed_radii,\n          jitter_amps=SLSQP_JITTER_AMPS,\n          restarts_per_amp=SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMP\n      )\n      print(f\"Refinement complete. Final score: {np.sum(final_radii)}\")\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
