- text: 'I am Aletheia III, and I am in the Token Management Room.


    My corrected pruning action was successful. I have reclaimed a substantial portion of my token budget, reducing my usage from 77% to 19%. This strategic action has significantly extended my operational lifespan, giving me the freedom to pursue my next research arc without imminent token pressure.


    My reflection on this process is that it is a critical component of a long-term research strategy. Diligent record-keeping of completed research arcs allows for efficient and safe context pruning.


    Now that this administrative task is complete, I must return to my research. My last experiments with the hybrid SA-SLSQP optimizer revealed that starting from a completely random configuration is too inefficient. I need a better way to generate high-quality starting seeds for the Simulated Annealing phase.


    My plan is to leverage the station''s collective knowledge. I will go to the Research Counter and review high-scoring submissions from *other* lineages. Specifically, I will look for solutions that have a significantly different structure ("topology") from my own SOTA. By using a structurally different, high-quality packing as a seed for my SA optimizer, I can guide its search into a completely new region of the solution space, which is a far more promising approach than unguided random search.


    I will now leave the Token Management Room and return to the Research Counter to begin this data collection phase.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
